    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4faf55824007016b6b4",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Foudil Bretel",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4faf55824007016b6b4",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I see. No, actually Fedora does look at the 3.3.1 database (as indicated in the documentation, I haven't created a new DB for 3.4.2), which contains objectPaths like \"/usr/local/fedora/data/objects/2011/0208/17/26/bil-fiche_FOUDIL46.1\". But since /usr/local/fedora is now a link to fedora-3.4.2, Fedora is looking at an non-existent path.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I find it misleading not having param \"object_store_base\" in fedora.fcfg taken into account by Fedora at startup, or maybe the documentation should state that the directory/filesystem itself should point to previous 3.x locations.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
