  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Looking at the error message, it is looking for file /usr/local/fedora-3.4.2/data/objects/2010/1005/15/54/fedora-system_ContentModel-3.0</p>\n\n<p>This looks like a path to your 3.4.2 objects, not 3.3.1.</p>\n\n<p>Fedora picks up the path from the SQL database, so it looks like it is not looking at the 3.3.1 database, but the 3.4.2 version.</p>",
     "created": "10/Mar/11 7:25 PM",
     "id": "11833",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10814/comment/11833",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "10/Mar/11 7:25 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4faf55824007016b6b4",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Foudil Bretel",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4faf55824007016b6b4",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I see. No, actually Fedora does look at the 3.3.1 database (as indicated in the documentation, I haven't created a new DB for 3.4.2), which contains objectPaths like \"/usr/local/fedora/data/objects/2011/0208/17/26/bil-fiche_FOUDIL46.1\". But since /usr/local/fedora is now a link to fedora-3.4.2, Fedora is looking at an non-existent path.</p>\n\n<p>I find it misleading not having param \"object_store_base\" in fedora.fcfg taken into account by Fedora at startup, or maybe the documentation should state that the directory/filesystem itself should point to previous 3.x locations.</p>",
     "created": "11/Mar/11 11:31 AM",
     "id": "11834",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10814/comment/11834",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4faf55824007016b6b4",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a513914e09f762ba75e178cc3d49e2e7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFB-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Foudil Bretel",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4faf55824007016b6b4",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "11/Mar/11 11:31 AM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>TBD: Document the workaround(s) we discussed on the March 15th committer call. Note that Akubra-fs does not store canonical paths so would seem to help with this kind of issue in the future.</p>",
     "created": "15/Mar/11 5:43 PM",
     "id": "11869",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10814/comment/11869",
     "updateAuthor": {
