  "description": "<p>1. have a previous 3.3.1 installation in /usr/local/fedora-3.3.1<br/>\n  have /usr/local/fedora-3.4.2 directory created<br/>\n  have /usr/local/fedora -&gt; fedora-3.4.2<br/>\n  have $FEDORA_HOME set to /usr/local/fedora</p>\n\n<p>2. follow instructions \"Upgrading from 3.x to 3.4.2\" on <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FCR30/Upgrading+from+3.x:\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FCR30/Upgrading+from+3.x:</a><br/>\n  (2.a) modify /usr/local/fedora-3.4.2/server/config/fedora.fcfg (fedora_db = DB for 3.3.1 instance):<br/>\n    &lt;param name=\"jdbcURL\" value=\"jdbc:mysql://localhost/fedora_db?useUnicode=true&amp;amp;characterEncoding=UTF-8&amp;amp;autoReconnect=true\"&gt;<br/>\n  (2.b) modify /usr/local/fedora-3.4.2/server/config/fedora.fcfg:<br/>\n   &lt;module role=\"org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.ILowlevelStorage\" class=\"org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.DefaultLowlevelStorageModule\"&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;param name=\"object_store_base\" value=\"../fedora-3.3.1/data/objects\" isFilePath=\"true\"&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;param name=\"datastream_store_base\" value=\"../fedora-3.3.1/data/datastreams\" isFilePath=\"true\"&gt;</p>\n\n<p>3. starting the new repository fails:</p>\n\n<p>org.fcrepo.server.errors.ServerInitializationException: Failed to ingest system object(s)<br/>\n...<br/>\nCaused by: org.fcrepo.server.errors.LowlevelStorageException: file /usr/local/fedora-3.4.2/data/objects/2010/1005/15/54/fedora-system_ContentModel-3.0doesn't exist for reading</p>\n\n<p>COMMENTS:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>using full-paths doesn't work either (value=\"/usr/local/fedora-3.3.1/data/objects\")</li>\n\t<li>possible solution: rebuild MySQL (and Resource Index ?) using fedora-rebuild.sh</li>\n</ul>\n",
